                'en' => 'Freight train no. 8957, which left Bourg at 2.37 pm with 22 wagons (326 tonnes), was hauled by a lead locomotive and pushed at the rear by a second engine, uncoupled. It came to a halt at about 7 pm, roughly 150 m below the summit. Local passenger train no. 1949, which left Bourg at 7.40 pm with over a hundred passengers and two locomotives, entered the tunnel at about 40 km/h after finding the signal open and struck the stopped train at about 8.50 pm.',
