                'en' => 'Funerals were held in Bourg and Ambérieu before large crowds; the PLM paid 20,000 francs to the families. The following month the company began building a ventilation station at the tunnel exit, blowing air against uphill trains. Train loads were reduced (by 25% for passenger trains, 50% for freight) and a ministerial circular on tunnel ventilation is dated 31 August 1922. The station was closed in 1955 with the arrival of diesel traction.',
